worktrees/

# Claude Code machine-local settings (allowlist shared in settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json

# session scratch + probe backups — NEVER track (s198 broad-add guard: the art
# runner's `git add -A` in the repo root swept these into bfadfc2, 4th instance).
# Ignoring them makes a repo-root -A safe-by-construction for future runs.
# `.s<N>-*` = per-fire scratch (line-1 backups, merge captures, probe helpers);
# covers all session numbers incl. legacy .s89/.s90/.s195 and future .s3xx.
.s[0-9]*
.s195-probe-bak/
scripts/_s*
playwright.s*.config.ts
.scratch/
# §3.0b gate worktrees (F-1608-3, s1609) — the SAME broad-add class as the block above,
# one directory over. §3.0b orders undecided content gated in a DETACHED WORKTREE, and the
# permission gate requires that worktree INSIDE the repo root, so every fire that obeys the
# law parks a nested repo at `gate-s<N>/` — where the ART slot's `git add -A` records it as a
# `160000` GITLINK: a submodule-shaped pointer to a commit no clone can resolve, at a path
# that stops existing the moment the worktree is removed. That is garbage in every future
# clone, and it survives review as one boring line in a 20-file art commit (s1608 caught
# `gate-s1608` -> `74bd34243` in `6c780b621` by eye, and removed it in `8b246eeeb`).
# The collision is STRUCTURAL, not one runner's slip — obeying §3.0b is what creates the dir.
# BLAST RADIUS MEASURED BEFORE LANDING, not assumed: `git ls-files | grep -E '^gate-'` = 0 at
# s1609, so this un-tracks NOTHING today and is purely forward-looking. `gate-s<N>` is the
# established convention (40+ fires, s1428..s1608); exactly one ever reached git.
# PROVED BY MANUFACTURING THE DEFECT in a throwaway repo, never by a broad add here — the
# hazard under test IS `git add -A` at a repo root: without the rule a real `worktree add
# --detach gate-s9999` stages as `160000` (the s1608 shape exactly); with it, skipped — and a
# CONTROL dir alongside is still added, so the rule cannot rot into an over-broad sweep.
gate-*/
# beauty-shift probe scratch (the-claim shift, 2026-08-02): throwaway page probes
# used to measure the sculpt before deciding an upgrade. The BOARDS are history and
# live in reviews/shots-beauty-claim/; these one-shot probes are not.
.scratch-beauty/
# THE EIGHT WINDS (2026-07-28): proof-only extraction of the diagonal siblings.
# Nothing binds these cells yet, so they must NOT reach assets/processed or the
# bundle — anim-pass-winds.mjs extracts here to measure and throws the cells away.
.scratch-ew/
# byte-identical copies another concurrent generation already owns (F-EW-2 repair).
reviews/eight-winds/gen/_misclaimed/
# ...but the codex banners ARE factory history (10b): each one records the session id
# that its image was claimed from, which is what makes every claim in the run files
# re-derivable. The repo-wide *.log rule at line 7 was swallowing them.
!reviews/eight-winds/gen/*.codex.log

# ...and the SAME rule was swallowing measurement evidence, which is the sibling case the
# negation above was written too narrow to cover (F-1573-1, s1573). A measurement task's raw
# per-run logs ARE its evidence: f1572-1 wrote 24 run-NN.log files whose review cited them by
# path, and only the 2-byte .rc companions reached git — silently, because `git status` shows
# an ignored file as nothing at all. That is a RETENTION LAW (CLAUDE.md 10b) hole: a drain can
# only re-derive a runner's numbers if the runner's raw output survives, and re-deriving them
# is exactly how the s1573 drain corroborated f1572-1 value-for-value.
# BLAST RADIUS MEASURED BEFORE LANDING, not assumed: at s1573 main's tree held 40 *.log files
# under artifacts/, ALL 40 already tracked, and `git ls-files --others --ignored` returned 0 —
# so this rule newly tracks NOTHING today and is purely forward-looking. Scoped to artifacts/
# on purpose: a blanket !**/*.log would sweep in every playwright/vite log repo-wide, which is
# the F-1027-2 black-hole shape. Reversible with one word.
!artifacts/**/*.log

# transient runner state — masters (tasks/*.md, tasks/BACKLOG.md) stay tracked,
# but queue/running/done/failed are ephemeral filesystem state the runner manages.
tasks/running/
tasks/done/
tasks/failed/
logs/.usage-census-cache.json
# generated each regen from the heredoc in scripts/dashboard-gen.sh (s1028, F-1028-1).
# Exact path on purpose — a wildcard here is how F-1027-2 turned logs/runs-archive/ into a black hole.
logs/.goal-tree.mjs
# scratch render targets for dashboard-gen.sh — a fire testing that script MUST redirect its output
# (GOLD_RUSH_DASHBOARD_OUT/_GOAL_TREE_TMP/_HEALTH_LOG) so a bad build can never clobber the live board.
# s1028 established the practice, s1031 used it for F-1028-2. Exact paths, never wildcards.
logs/.scratch-dashboard.html
logs/.scratch-goal-tree.html
logs/.scratch-goal-tree.mjs
logs/.scratch-health.log
# dry-board guard counter written by scripts/fire-runner.sh:53. Untracked runtime state, but three
# consecutive handoffs had to explain it as unexplained dirt — ignoring it ends that (s1025 flagged it).
tasks/.fire-skip-count
rehearsal-video/
rider-video/
# E1 depth-review footage + per-map fresh profiles (TASK 2026-07-25: local video class).
e1-review-video/
# Standing-orders rehearsal (TASK 2026-07-30): fresh browser profiles are local play state, never
# history. The rider transcripts + meters under rehearsal/so-runs/ ARE committed as evidence.
rehearsal-profile/
rehearsal-profile-*/
TASK.md

# build scratch — wrangler regenerates these per dev run (F-1154-1, s1154)
.wrangler/

# Python bytecode caches (F-1298-1, s1298). env/goldrush-verifiers is the repo's first tracked
# Python package and its lane commit carried two committed .pyc blobs (cpython-311, ~30 KB) because
# nothing ignored them. They are interpreter- and version-specific build debris, they rot against the
# 3.10+ floor the package declares, and they are regenerated on every import. The two from that
# commit were withheld at the drain rather than merged; this rule stops the class, not the instance.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
env/goldrush-verifiers/.venv/
